  "protocol": "Seven alternating fresh-Node sets; 24 pinned Kodak photos. Kernel: prepared hashes/source decoding excluded; 25 warmup batches then 500 timed batches=12000 owned 16x16 RGBA results, consumed by checksum. Reference blurhash2.0.5; cachedJS caches base83/cosine/sRGB/coefficients but uses reference power gamma; thresholdJS additionally uses same 2048-bin gamma hint/255 thresholds/conservative 1e-7 boundary fallback as Rust. Rust includes ASCII copy/validation, exact boundary fallback and owned pixel copy. Incremental initialization excludes common imports; native gamma tables initialize lazily in first batch, JS controls initialize during factory setup. Complete previews: no preview-cache reuse, first24-photo batch, one warmup,72timed sequential operations; complete JSON digest must match. LQIP/ThumbHash unchanged controls. All suites serial on uncontrolled desktop.",
